  "question": {
    "text": "The line \\(3 x-4 y+7=0\\) is rotated through an angle \\(\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\) in the clockwise direction about the point \\((-1,1)\\). The equation of the line in its new position is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "W78Fo",
      "text": "\\(7 y+x-6=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iJr6t",
      "text": "\\(7 y-x-6=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "G8IfM",
      "text": "\\(7 y+x+6=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "awbcj",
      "text": "\\(7 y-x+6=0\\)",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As \\((-1,1)\\) is a point on \\(3 x-4 y+7=0\\), the rotation is possible. Slope of the given line \\(=3 / 4\\). Slope of the line in its new position\n\\(=\\frac{\\frac{3}{4}-1}{1+\\frac{3}{4}}=-\\frac{1}{7}\\)\nThe required equation is\n\\(\\mathrm{y}-1=-\\frac{1}{7}(\\mathrm{x}+1) \\text { or } 7 \\mathrm{y}+\\mathrm{x}-6=0\\)",
    "image": null
  },
